                "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 26 at 1:12PM AKST until November 28 at 6:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Coastal Flooding with water levels 1.5 to 3.0 feet\nabove the highest tide line possible.\n\n* WHERE...Kipnuk, Kongiganak, and Kwigillingok.\n\n* WHEN...6 PM Today to 6 AM Saturday. Particularly the overnight\nhigh tide tonight and Friday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Potential flooding of low lying areas, including\nlowest portions of boardwalks. Coastal erosion possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A long duration of onshore winds combined\nwith higher-than-normal tides will increase the potential for\nelevated water levels, high surf, and coastal erosion tonight\nand Friday night. Tides will remain higher than normal into the\nmiddle of next week.",
                "instruction": "A coastal flood advisory indicates that onshore winds and tides\nwill combine to generate flooding of low areas along the shore.",
                "response": "Monitor",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
