                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued November 26 at 1:04PM AKST until November 27 at 6:00PM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Snow and blowing snow expected. Total snow accumulations 3\nto 6 inches. Winds gusting as high as 40 to 50 mph. Visibilities\nreduced to one half mile or less due to blowing snow.\n\n* WHERE...Kuskokwim Delta Coast and Nunivak Island.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM AKST Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Areas of blowing snow could\nsignificantly reduce visibility.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Highest chances of blowing snow are on Nunivak\nIsland and along the Kuskokwim Delta Coast north of Kipnuk.\nSoutheast winds become westerly early Friday morning. The strongest\nwind gusts are expected Friday morning after winds become westerly.\nConditions are expected to gradually improve late Friday afternoon\nas snowfall tapers off and winds begin to decrease.",
                "instruction": "Use caution while traveling.",
                "response": "Execute",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
