                "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued November 26 at 10:28AM AKST until November 28 at 9:00AM AKST by NWS Fairbanks AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Snow and blowing snow expected. Total snow accumulations up\nto two inches. Winds gusting up to 40 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Bering Strait Coast, Interior Seward Peninsula, Diomede,\nand Southern Seward Peninsula Coast.\n\n* WHEN...From 3 PM Friday to 9 AM AKST Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel may be impacted. Blowing and falling snow could\nreduce visibility to 1/2 mile or less at times.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Snow totals of 0.5 to 2 inches expected for\nmost locations. South facing slopes along the southern Seward\nPeninsula including near Nome could see up to 3 inches of snow.\nWinds peak overnight Friday into Saturday and rapidly weaken\nthrough Saturday.",
